- Fixed `fleetctl gitops` silently skipping `org_settings.mdm.end_user_license_agreement` on servers where Apple MDM is not configured. The EULA is part of the setup experience and is not Apple-only, so it now applies whenever any MDM platform is turned on. `fleetctl generate-gitops` exports it in the same cases, so a generated configuration no longer deletes an uploaded EULA when re-applied. When the EULA cannot be applied, because the server is on Fleet Free or has no MDM turned on, gitops now reports that instead of ignoring the setting silently.
- Fixed the end user license agreement (EULA) section being hidden in Settings > Integrations > MDM on servers where Apple MDM is not configured, so a EULA can now be uploaded, viewed, and deleted on Fleet Premium servers using Windows or Android MDM.
